WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.046 --> 00:00:05.523
One day a merchant was walking home from the market.

2
00:00:05.524 --> 00:00:10.172
He had loaded big bags of salt on his donkey's back.

3
00:00:10.173 --> 00:00:16.409
"Oh my. This salt is so heavy," the donkey thought.

4
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:23.713
"It will be a long, hard trip home."

5
00:00:23.714 --> 00:00:27.049
Soon they came to a stream.

6
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:31.183
As they entered the water, the donkey slipped.

7
00:00:31.184 --> 00:00:35.600
Splash! He fell into the stream.

8
00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:41.799
When the donkey stood, his load felt much lighter.

9
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.995
"That's odd," he thought.

10
00:00:44.996 --> 00:00:49.731
"Oh no, my salt!" the merchant cried.

11
00:00:49.732 --> 00:00:55.261
"All my salt is gone!" He sighed.

12
00:00:55.262 --> 00:00:58.306
"What an unlucky day."

13
00:00:58.307 --> 00:01:02.727
Meanwhile the tired donkey was delighted.

14
00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:08.497
"What a lucky day!" he thought, laughing aloud.

15
00:01:08.498 --> 00:01:12.722
"Hee-haw! Hee-haw!"

16
00:01:12.723 --> 00:01:17.745
Soon they went to the market for salt again.

17
00:01:17.746 --> 00:01:22.325
On the way home, they had to cross the stream again.

18
00:01:22.326 --> 00:01:26.749
"I know what to do!" the donkey thought.

19
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:33.800
This time he fell into the water on purpose. Splash!

20
00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:38.017
"That's better!" the donkey thought as he stood.

21
00:01:38.018 --> 00:01:41.609
"My load is so much lighter now!"

22
00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:45.953
He laughed aloud. "Hee-haw! Hee-haw!"

23
00:01:45.954 --> 00:01:52.210
By now the merchant was growing suspicious of his donkey.

24
00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:57.594
The next time they went to market, he bought bags of sponges.

25
00:01:57.595 --> 00:02:02.602
He loaded them onto the donkey, and they headed home.

26
00:02:02.603 --> 00:02:07.023
"This is not a very heavy load," the donkey thought.

27
00:02:07.024 --> 00:02:11.407
"But I know a way to make it even lighter!"

28
00:02:11.408 --> 00:02:18.220
While they crossed the stream, the donkey fell into the water. Splash!

29
00:02:18.221 --> 00:02:22.004
"I'm so clever!" the donkey thought.

30
00:02:22.005 --> 00:02:28.142
The merchant frowned. "Stand up, donkey!"

31
00:02:28.143 --> 00:02:33.277
But when the donkey tried to stand, he could barely move.

32
00:02:33.278 --> 00:02:39.855
"What happened?" he thought. "My load grew so heavy!"

33
00:02:39.856 --> 00:02:44.058
"Now the sponges are full of water," the merchant said.

34
00:02:44.059 --> 00:02:49.074
"That will teach you a lesson. Let's go."

35
00:02:49.075 --> 00:02:57.455
Finally the donkey managed to stand.

36
00:02:57.456 --> 00:03:02.909
"I was foolish," he thought as they started walking again.

37
00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:06.222
"Now my load is much heavier.

38
00:03:06.223 --> 00:03:09.836
I must remember not to play tricks.

39
00:03:09.837 --> 00:03:16.705
I don't like it when others play tricks on me!"

